  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion:centered-domain-poincare",
    "anchor": "PBPS arXiv2609.06905v1 global source assumptions HTML98-100, Section2.2 HTML168-212, AppendixC1 HTML1197-1237 and background D6/D9 HTML1601-1630; actual reflected conditional score variance. SPHMC2609.06906v1 Section4.1 HTML403-430 has a separate future unreflected covariance consumer. Independent primary-first Centered_Poincare_source_preread.md.",
    "original_text": "Exact independently sealed bounded statement:\nFinite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel full E including0. Actual C2 potential W, ordinary-volume exp(-W) integrability and positive partition. Actual normalized probability mu=volume.tilted(-W).\nBOTH actual global mI<=HessW<=MI and0<m<=M. SAME exact original compact-smooth closable weighted gradient D BEFORE ALL mean-zero z in D.closure.domain. No input Poincare or supplied resolvent/coercivity/limit certificate. This canonical library contract is narrower than lower-only source D6.\nFor every genuinely centered z in the SAME original closed weighted-gradient domain, prove m*normz^2<=normDclosurez^2 from actual positive-epsilon solutions, SAME variational uniqueness, global coercivity and true strong scaled residual limit.\nFinite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel full E including0, genuine C2 W with actual exponential integrability/positive partition, normalized tilted probability, BOTH global mI<=HessW<=MI and0<m<=M. SAME original exact compact-smooth closable weighted gradient D BEFORE all truly mean-zero domain z. Actual positiveepsilon variational solutions from residual/globalcoercivity producers are identified by SAME D/epsilon/forcing uniqueness, then tested against z; strong scaled residual limit and genuine scalar Cauchy-Schwarz/zero-norm branch give m*normz^2<=normDclosurez^2. No uniform unscaled solution bound, centered resolvent, epsilon0 solution, core/range/adjoint certificate or input Poincare. Actual C1 scalar/gradientL2 pairs and centered function are admitted to a genuine original graph, actual probability/AE quotient identities and real integrability produce Admissible and m*Var<=DirichletEnergy. Actual common Gaussian J/R/S, sourceC2 alpha-beta eta cap, reflected W_y, positive partitions and one original D_y precede allcentered z/score directions; actual unnormalized parameter-y score variance <=(eta^-1-alpha)^2*norma^2/(4*(alpha+eta^-1)), with exact reflected m=(alpha+eta^-1)/4 and source-derived upper M=(beta+eta^-1)/4. Auxiliary normalized density equality only; no R2=R/alternateD identification/jointselector or normalized conditional density derivative. BOTH-curvature generic statement is narrower than lower-only source D6 and is disclosed; source companion models supply the upper bound. Anisotropic BL, unreflected linear moments/covariance-upper and SPHMC Hessian lower, outer-y/marginal Poincare, PBPS sampler/reflection/invariance/nonexplosion/hypocoercivity/implementation/cost, SPHMC complete algorithm/Wp/proxywarmness, main results/composition/expectedcost remainopen. TV does not transfer unbounded cost.",
    "text_sha256": "2839d3bf10754c9b3f05bbe2cd13882b916cde8d3f0879eeb3e865e053ef486f"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.CenteredDomainPoincare.gibbs_centered_domain_poincare",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/FunctionalInequalities/CenteredDomainPoincare.lean",
    "statement": "{E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    (W : E → ℝ) (hW : ContDiff ℝ 2 W)\n    (hI : Integrable (fun x => Real.exp (-W x)))\n    (hZ : 0 < ∫ x, Real.exp (-W x))\n    (m M : ℝ) (hm : 0 < m) (hmM : m ≤ M)\n    (hlower : ∀ x a, m*‖a‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ W) x a a)\n    (hupper : ∀ x a, fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ W) x a a ≤ M*‖a‖^2) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -W x)\n    ∀ (D : Lp ℝ 2 μ →ₗ.[ℝ] Lp E 2 μ), D.IsClosable →\n      (∀ (a : Lp ℝ 2 μ) (G : Lp E 2 μ), (a,G) ∈ D.graph ↔\n        ∃ φ : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ ∞ φ ∧ HasCompactSupport φ ∧\n          a =ᵐ[μ] φ ∧ G =ᵐ[μ] gradient φ) →\n      ∀ z : D.closure.domain, (∫ x, (z : Lp ℝ 2 μ) x ∂μ)=0 →\n        m*‖(z : Lp ℝ 2 μ)‖^2 ≤ ‖D.closure z‖^2",
    "statement_sha256": "be3c9abf9fc64e21d6fd067318dcd0bbcbf0bc439aaa9b3fce5dc5e733639e2e",
    "compiled": true
  },
  "blind_reconstruction": {
    "text": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with NormedAddCommGroup,InnerProductSpace R,FiniteDimensional R,MeasurableSpace,BorelSpace instances and canonical full-space volume,including dimension zero. Let W:E->R be C2 and assume exp(-W) is volume-integrable and its volume integral strictly positive. Let m,M:R satisfy m>0 and m<=M. Assume for EVERY x,a:E BOTH genuine all-point/all-vector bounds\n  m*||a||^2 <= (fderiv R (fderiv R W) x a) a,\n  (fderiv R (fderiv R W) x a) a <= M*||a||^2.\nDefine mu=volume.tilted(x->-W(x)),the actual normalized exp(-W)/positive partition measure.\nFor EVERY original real-linear partial operator D:Lp R 2 mu->partialLinear[R] Lp E 2 mu,assume D.IsClosable and the exact graph iff: for every scalar L2 class b and vector L2 class G,(b,G) belongs to D.graph iff there exists a smooth compactly supported real phi with b=phi mu-AE and G=gradient(phi) mu-AE. D.closure is the actual closure of this same original graph on its submodule domain.\nThen for EVERY z:D.closure.domain satisfying the actual centered condition integral (z as scalar L2 representative)(x) dmu(x)=0,\n  m*||z as Lp R 2 mu||^2 <= ||D.closure(z)||^2.\nThese are genuine weighted scalar/vector quotient L2 norms. D is fixed before all centered z,not selected anew per input. Mean zero is with respect to actual mu;no assumed Poincare/coercivity/limit certificate or resolvent witness is an input. The original graph's smooth test functions have compact support,but z is a general actual closure-domain element without a compact-support condition. Both lower and upper C2 curvature assumptions are retained;this is not a lower-only contract. The inequality is output for every such centered z,not a premise. No probability-law change,pointwise rough Hessian,anisotropic Hessian-inverse inequality,joint measurable operator choice,normalized-score derivative,marginal inequality or main/cost composition statement is asserted.",
    "text_sha256": "2c415872c5645bff7d163a753c9a60911cbd9fffcb922e3a91e71880712f7270",
    "decoder": "anonymous_decoder_20261006",
    "decoder_packet_sha256": "daad7a311a506c25ef0bfd34200b2f5455805e9e4db805c8804631a37e6bb47f",
